{
  "dom_id": "step-q345016",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14195167/assets/0ef7a2645946099b10772fdc3fee46c582ad43debb0cb53041c46aa99c203ab1.png)\n\nSofia is designing a park that is made up of a rectangle and two semicircles, as shown in the diagram. The area of the park must be $16\\,{km}^{2}.$ What should be the radius $r$ if Sofia wants a park with the smallest possible perimeter? Do not round the answer.\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{km}$",
  "worked_solution": "We let $r$ be the radius of the circular sector (the same for both semicircles) and let $x$ be the other side of the rectangle. Then, we want to minimize the perimeter\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =2x+\\pi r+\\pi r \\\\  & =2x+2\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the area is fixed at $16\\text{ km},$ so we also have the constraint condition\n\n$$\n16=2rx+\\pi {r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, by making $2x$ the subject of the constraint equation and taking into account that $r>0,$ we find that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 & =2rx+\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 2rx & =16-\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{16}{r}-\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging this into our expression for $P,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\frac{16}{r}-\\pi r+2\\pi r \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{r}+\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to minimize $P,$ so we need to differentiate $P$ and set the derivative equal to zero. Computing the derivative gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(r) & =-\\frac{16}{{r}^{2}}+\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the derivative equal to zero and solving for $r$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{16}{{r}^{2}}+\\pi  & =0 \\\\ \\pi  & =\\frac{16}{{r}^{2}} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{16}{\\pi } \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{\\pi }} \\\\ r & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we confirm that $\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}$ is a minimum using the second derivative test.\n\nSince the second derivative ${P}^{″}(r)=\\frac{32}{{r}^{3}}>0,$ the stationary point $r=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}\\,\\text{km}$ is a minimum.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
